    "The Khmer alphabet for SquirrelGo Alphabets. A consonant's romanization is its name: ka for the first series (built-in vowel aa), ko for the second (built-in vowel oo). Example romanizations are a simplified UNGEGN style. eSpeak NG has no Khmer voice, so the sounds are made from the IPA. Hints, groupings and articles are original."
